{
  "name": "services",
  "integration": "tenable-ot-security",
  "description": "Open ports. The path is Asset.directNetworkInterfaces -> NetworkInterface.ips -> IpDetails.openPorts -> IPOpenPorts.ports -> OpenPorts { port scanTime source name description }. Because the ports hang off one IpDetails rather than off the asset, every service lands on the address the console actually saw it on -- 0001 has two interfaces and its 44818 must sit on 10.180.7.10 while its 502 sits on 10.180.8.10, which no flat port list could express. OpenPorts publishes a port and the protocol most likely spoken on it but NO transport, so tcp is assumed and the assumption is recorded as transport_source rather than presented as reported fact. The block is opt-in because it is the deepest selection in the document, three connections down, and this fixture is the only one that asks for it: the others assert openPorts is absent from the request entirely. The junk rows are the point of 0001's second interface: port 0 and port 70000 are outside the legal range and must be dropped rather than emitted as implausible services, and 502 appears twice on the same address and must be deduplicated to one service. 0002 has an interface whose only address is loopback, so its ports must not become services on an address that identifies nothing, and the asset must still import on its flat directIps -- 127.0.0.1 never reaches an interface, so an asset that had only that would have no correlator at all.",
